# Admin Documentation & Content Guide

> **Important**: This guide explains how to populate the empty sections of your site and details the capabilities of the Tier 5 Admin Features you have enabled.

## 1. Why are my pages empty?

Even with features enabled, the public pages (e.g., `/blog`, `/speaking`, `/downloads`) will appear empty until you **create and publish content** via the Admin Panel.

### How to Add Content
1.  Go to **Admin Dashboard** (`/admin`).
2.  Navigate to the relevant section (e.g., **Blog**, **Speaking**, **Downloads**, **Testimonials**).
3.  Click the **+ New Post** (or similar "New") button.
4.  Fill in the form.
5.  **Critical Step**: For the content to appear on the public site, you must check the **Publish** checkbox (or set Status to "Published").
6.  Click **Save**.

Once saved and published, refresh the public page to see your content immediately.

