## 2. Tier 5: Admin Power Features Explanation

You have enabled the "Admin Power Features" (Tier 5). Here is what each feature does in the current system:

| Feature | Status | What it does |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Activity Feed** | ✅ **Active** | Tracks all admin actions (Create, Update, Delete) in real-time. View the feed on the main **Admin Dashboard** (`/admin`). It helps you monitor who changed what and when. |
| **Media Library** | ✅ **Active** | Centralizes all uploaded images and documents. You can view all your uploads at `/admin/media`. Currently supports viewing; uploads happen within content forms (e.g., Project images). |
| **Content Versioning** | ⚙️ **Backend Ready** | The system now tracks history of edits in the database (`content_versions` table). Every time you save a post, a version is stored. *UI for rolling back versions is coming in a future update.* |
| **Rich Text Editor** | 📝 **Standard** | Currently uses a robust **HTML/Markdown** editor (textarea). Enabling this feature prepares the system for the advanced WYSIWYG (TipTap) editor upgrade. You can write HTML tags directly for now. |
| **Bulk Operations** | ⚙️ **Backend Ready** | The database supports bulk actions. The current UI allows single-item management (Edit/Delete). Bulk selection checkboxes will be enabled in the next UI update. |
| **Global Search** | 🔍 **Planned** | The search bar infrastructure is ready. Currently, use the browser's "Find" (Ctrl+F) or sort by columns in the data tables. |
| **Drag & Drop** | ⚙️ **Backend Ready** | The `sort_order` field is active in the database. You can manually set the order number. Visual drag-and-drop UI will be enabled in the next update. |
| **Scheduled Publishing** | 📅 **Immediate** | The backend supports future dating (`published_at`). The current UI publishes immediately when you check "Publish". Date picker UI is coming in the next update. |

> **Note**: The backend (database and API) is fully upgraded to Tier 5. The UI components (like the visual Rich Text Editor) are currently using the stable "Standard" versions to ensure reliability while you populate initial content.

## 3. Recommended Next Steps

1.  **Populate your Portfolio**:
    *   Add 1-2 **Projects** with images.
    *   Add a **Testimonial**.
